|~ What is declared under `::bind`, the step that declares a name:
   the refusals of a declaration. ~|

:bind/BindPayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::bind` is a map of `:name`, a keyword or a tag, `:docs`, a
      vector of docs, and `:body`, a step.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        ::bind{:name :inc :docs [1]}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::bind/BindPayloadNotSchemaError :docs]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:bind/BindReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The ::bind prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      declaration binds a body or docs, and a body that is a keyword
      or a tag is written as a group.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        ::bind{:name :inc}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::bind/BindReadBackDiffersError ":inc"]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:bind/EffectLaunderingAtBindStepParseError
  |~~ A verb whose body calls a name marked `@` reaches outside the
      language, and its own name carries the mark, `:@fetchAll
      ::verb~(@fetch …)`, so every reader of the name sees it.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        1 | (:bad ::verb~(@callers) | bad)
        !| [type /bindingName /effectfulName]
        |  eq [::bind/EffectLaunderingAtBindStepParseError
                :bad :@callers]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:bind/BindVerbSubjectUnderKindError
  |~~ A verb declared under a kind serves that kind: the kind is its
      subject, and its head names none of its own. A verb under a noun
      that is no kind, a topic, serves any value.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        :Box ::spec~() | :Box/area ::verb~(:subject ::map | 1)
        !| [type /name]
        |  eq [::bind/BindVerbSubjectUnderKindError :Box/area]
       )
      ~(:t {} | :t/h ::verb~(type) | 5 | t/h | eq ::number)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:bind/BindNounNotDeclaredError
  |~~ A name with a path is declared under the noun its path names
      before its last name, and that noun is declared before it, so
      whether the noun is a kind, which the verbs under it serve, is
      known where they are declared.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(:Box/area ::verb~(1) !| [type /noun] | eq [::bind/BindNounNotDeclaredError ::Box])
      ~(:Box ::spec~() | :Box/area ::verb~(1) | ::Box{} | area | eq 1)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:bind/BindNameDeclaredTwiceError
  |~~ A name is declared once in a scope: the steps of a pipeline
      that the pipe or the fail track joins share one env, and a
      declaration of a name one of them declared before is refused
      where it stands. A group, an element, a modifier, a quote and
      a step joined by `*` open scopes of their own, where a name
      of the scope around them is shadowed. An address the root
      holds is declared once at all: a reader extends a noun of the
      root and replaces none of its nodes, and a source of the root
      that declares a name the root holds is refused.
      ::link~(::bind | doc)

      ~(
        :k 1 | :k 2
        !| [type /name]
        |  eq [::bind/BindNameDeclaredTwiceError :k]
       )
      ~(:k 1 | (:k 2 | k) | eq 2)
      ~(:vec/count ::verb~(0) !| type | eq ::bind/BindNameDeclaredTwiceError)
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
